      <rules>
        <rule id="752d-71a2-003b-c02a" name="Treeman allowance — manual check" hidden="false">
          <description>One Treeman per complete 1,000 points of agreed army size (Wood Elves p. 68). Check this against the battle limit; this release does not infer it from points spent.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="67cc-3327-331b-e17d" name="Model count" hidden="false">
          <description>Models includes troopers, standard bearer, musician and champion. Command models replace troopers; they do not upgrade a model already counted. Whole-unit options automatically charge every model; champions pay character equipment rates.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
    </selectionEntry>
    <selectionEntry id="5ad0-cb2b-f698-4d16" name="Chariot" type="model" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" publicationId="2e06-8dc0-e774-819f" page="66">
      <costs>
        <cost name="pts" typeId="0044-15f1-782b-00ea" value="76" />
      </costs>
      <categoryLinks>
        <categoryLink id="29de-d5ce-3385-7697" name="Regiments" targetId="a2b5-2a83-607e-e007" primary="true" hidden="false" />
      </categoryLinks>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink id="cd6e-ff93-55ac-af74" name="Chariots" targetId="4aec-6ebc-71f0-fd54" type="rule" hidden="false" publicationId="d7c9-7773-4408-58f6" page="75–77" />
      </infoLinks>
      <rules>
        <rule id="8a8a-f005-5a1a-9ae9" name="Wood Elf chariot movement" hidden="false">
          <description>Chariots do not benefit from the Wood Elf ability to ignore woodland movement penalties. Wood Elves p. 66.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="0401-1463-ddf3-1b1e" name="Chariot impact Strength" hidden="false">
          <description>The Wood Elf chariot profile prints a dash for Strength (Wood Elves p. 66). The core chariot rule gives Strength 7 in most cases (Rulebook p. 77). Use that core value for impact hits unless an agreed clarification says otherwise; the displayed army-book profile is preserved.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="e0c2-e266-331d-c624" name="Chariot equipment" hidden="false">
          <description>76 points includes two crew with hand weapons/light armour and two steeds. Crew upgrades are paid per crewman. A character replaces the optional third crewman. See Wood Elves p. 66. Chariot magic standards are pending, to avoid a duplicate army-wide allowance across mounts and units.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="d928-f819-f08d-33bc" name="Chariot regiments" hidden="false">
          <description>Select each chariot separately and identify its regiment in roster notes. A chariot-regiment champion is not implemented in this release.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <profiles>
        <profile id="c16c-df95-74fd-d22a" name="Chariot" typeId="e25d-f63f-8d67-4bda" typeName="Unit" hidden="false" publicationId="2e06-8dc0-e774-819f" page="66">
