          </characteristics>
        </profile>
        <profile id="a619-f115-6d2b-bc84" name="Binding Bolas" typeId="b93a-4f1c-9871-3028" typeName="Magic item" hidden="false" publicationId="2e06-8dc0-e774-819f" page="80">
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Type" typeId="7ef9-9797-693d-d937">Enchanted item</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Effect" typeId="d277-fc43-48d0-6dce">One use, range 12 inches, BS to hit, Strength 4 and -1 armour save. May target characters. If a wound is saved by armour, the victim cannot move next turn; its unit moves at its slowest member’s speed.</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Reference" typeId="2fa3-15cf-fc7d-e42b">Woodelves, printed p. 80. Card value 10 points, included in the character total.</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Coverage" typeId="23f7-abf1-238e-1daa">Book-checked summary; fixed loadout</characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <constraints>
        <constraint id="4515-a153-0872-cb6e" type="max" value="1" scope="parent" field="selections" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" />
        <constraint id="ab46-62f2-e4da-a97e" type="max" value="1" scope="roster" field="selections" percentValue="false" shared="true" includeChildSelections="true" includeChildForces="false" />
      </constraints>
      <rules>
        <rule id="979a-2ae1-9ef4-89a4" name="Special character" hidden="false">
          <description>Unique named selection. 166 points includes the complete listed fixed equipment, companions, powers and mounts; only separately offered options add points. Printed profiles are before magic-item bonuses unless a rule says they are already included. Special-character use requires the players’ agreement under the books’ convention.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="7109-9530-a044-4edb" name="Included equipment" hidden="false">
          <description>Hand weapon; animal-hide cape (5+ armour).</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="2282-4f28-ff48-8ef9" name="Beastmaster and tigers" hidden="false" publicationId="2e06-8dc0-e774-819f" page="80">
          <description>The 66-point pair is included. Tigers move separately but must stay within 12 inches for control and use his Leadership. Both pack and master ignore Panic. A charge requires the target visible to both pack and master; he need not join it. Beyond 12 inches or after his death, tigers scatter and charge the nearest enemy in reach. They never attack Wood Elves. Tigers can break and rally. If both die, Gruarth hates the enemy. Missile hits against the combined group: 5–6 Gruarth, otherwise tigers. Reference: Woodelves, printed p. 80.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink id="df8a-5da8-60f3-cf70" name="Hand weapon" targetId="f660-63e8-377a-579c" type="rule" hidden="false" publicationId="d7c9-7773-4408-58f6" page="54" />
      </infoLinks>
    </selectionEntry>
